---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceAreaMap from '../../components/ServiceAreaMap.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { serviceNode } from '../../lib/schema';

const title = 'PDR Service Area | Greeley & Northern Colorado';
const description = 'See Peak Country’s standard 25-mile mobile-service area around downtown Greeley and learn how professional mobile PDR is scheduled throughout Northern Colorado.';
const serviceAreas = [{ '@type': 'City', name: 'Greeley, Colorado' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Weld County, Colorado' }, ...site.approvedCommunities.filter((name) => name !== 'Greeley').map((name) => ({ '@type': 'City', name: `${name}, Colorado` })), { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Northern Colorado' }];
const pageSchema = serviceNode('/service-area/','Mobile Paintless Dent Repair Service',description,serviceAreas);
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} exactTitle pageSchema={pageSchema} socialImage={{src:'/brand/hero-storm-background-1942.webp',width:1942,height:809,alt:'Northern Colorado mountain and storm landscape',type:'image/webp'}}>
  <header class="page-head area-head"><div class="eyebrow">Mobile service · By appointment</div><h1>Professional mobile PDR throughout Northern Colorado</h1><p>Mobile service is designed around convenience without compromising the conditions needed for a quality repair.</p><div class="about-actions"><a class="button" href="/get-started/">Get Started →</a><a class="text-link" href={`tel:${site.phone}`}>Call {site.phoneDisplay} →</a></div></header>
  <section class="section area-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">Service area, not a storefront</div><h2>Clear travel expectations, <span>without a geographic gate</span></h2><p>Peak Country is a mobile, by-appointment PDR service. The standard mobile-service area is approximately a <strong>{site.mobileServiceArea.radiusMiles}-mile geographic radius from a fixed neutral reference point in downtown Greeley, Colorado.</strong></p><p>The circle represents the area where standard mobile travel is included where applicable. It is not measured from city limits, and it does not define the full area where customers may start a conversation or request service.</p></div><aside><strong>Still outside the circle?</strong><p>That is okay. Mobile service may still be available. Any small mobile-service fee is discussed before scheduling—never assumed or added as a surprise.</p></aside></section>
  <ServiceAreaMap />
  <section class="area-band"><div class="section area-terms"><div><div class="eyebrow">What the circle means</div><h2>Inside the standard area</h2><p>Standard mobile travel is included where applicable. The map gives a consistent geographic reference for discussing the repair location, not a promise that every repair can be completed outdoors or at every site.</p></div><div><div class="eyebrow">Outside the standard area</div><h2>Still contact Peak Country</h2><p>Depending on distance, repair scope, service required, and scheduling circumstances, a small mobile-service fee may apply. We will discuss any additional fee before scheduling. Location alone never prevents a customer from requesting an assessment.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section area-communities"><div><div class="eyebrow">Northern Colorado communities</div><h2>Named areas for clarity</h2><p>These communities help customers find the right information and describe the Northern Colorado area where Peak Country regularly discusses mobile PDR. They do not determine whether standard included mobile travel applies—the radius does.</p></div><ul aria-label="Primary named service areas">{site.approvedCommunities.map((name) => <li>{name}</li>)}</ul></section>
  <section class="section mobile-standard"><div class="mobile-standard-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Professional Mobile PDR</div><h2>Convenience with the right conditions for the work</h2><p>Many repairs can be completed at a home, workplace, fleet facility, dealership, commercial location, or another suitable location. When conditions support the work, Peak Country brings the repair to you. When a more controlled environment will provide a better evaluation or repair, we will recommend it.</p><p>Indoor or covered environments are preferred when practical because controlled lighting, temperature, cleanliness, and weather protection can improve the repair process and final evaluation.</p></div><div class="mobile-standard-cards"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Weather and workspace</h3><p>Outdoor repairs may be possible when weather and workspace conditions allow. Normal outdoor repair should not occur in rain or snow. Excessive wind may require relocation or rescheduling, and temperatures below approximately 50–60°F may require a different location or time depending on the repair.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>What Peak Country brings</h3><p>Professional PDR lighting and the equipment needed for the work come with the technician. Customer electrical power is not normally required, and normal removal and installation work may be performed mobile when appropriate.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>What helps the appointment go smoothly</h3><p>A reasonably clean, dry vehicle and reasonable working access support an accurate assessment and careful repair. Keys and authorization to move or reposition the vehicle may be needed; the customer does not need to remain with the vehicle when the needed access and authorization are arranged.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Hail work</h3><p>Hail damage commonly involves a larger, panel-by-panel evaluation and generally benefits from—or requires—a controlled indoor environment. That recommendation is about the vehicle and the repair conditions, not a barrier to starting the conversation.</p></div></article></div></section>
  <section class="section area-links"><div><div class="eyebrow">Start with a conversation</div><h2>Not sure whether mobile service fits your repair?</h2><p>Tell us about the vehicle and the damage. Photos are helpful but not required to begin. We can discuss location and the conditions that will support the best evaluation or repair—without creating an automatic geographic yes-or-no.</p></div><nav aria-label="Related services and local hail information"><a class="button" href="/get-started/">Get Started →</a><a href="/auto-hail-repair/">Auto Hail Repair →</a><a href="/paintless-dent-repair/">Paintless Dent Repair →</a><a href="/repair-standards/">Repair Standards →</a><a href="/hail-tracker/greeley/">Greeley Hail Reports →</a><a href="/hail-tracker/weld-county/">Weld County Hail Reports →</a><a href="/hail-tracker/northern-colorado/">Northern Colorado Hail Reports →</a></nav></section>
  <div class="area-mountain-transition" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <script>
    const reducedMotion=window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
    const revealTargets=[...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.area-intro,.service-map-section,.area-band,.area-communities,.mobile-standard,.area-links')];
    const revealAll=()=>revealTargets.forEach(target=>target.classList.add('is-visible'));
    if(reducedMotion.matches||!('IntersectionObserver'in window))revealAll();
    else{
      document.documentElement.classList.add('service-area-motion-ready');
      const observer=new IntersectionObserver((entries)=>entries.forEach(entry=>{if(entry.isIntersecting){entry.target.classList.add('is-visible');observer.unobserve(entry.target);}}),{rootMargin:'0px 0px -7%'});
      revealTargets.forEach(target=>{target.dataset.serviceAreaReveal='';observer.observe(target);});
      reducedMotion.addEventListener('change',event=>{if(event.matches){observer.disconnect();revealAll();}});
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
